@gatewayBaseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Scenario 32
### User deactivation publishes an auth event and claim-service closes active claims asynchronously

### 32.1 Login as landlord and admin
# @name loginLandlord
POST {{gatewayBaseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1
}

###
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{gatewayBaseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 5
}

### 32.2 Create a claim
# @name createClaim
POST {{gatewayBaseUrl}}/api/claims
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginLandlord.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "tenantUserId": 3,
  "title": "Deactivation demo claim",
  "description": "This claim should be closed when the tenant is deactivated.",
  "claimedAmount": 70.00,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### 32.3 Deactivate the tenant while the claim is still active
POST {{gatewayBaseUrl}}/api/auth/users/3/deactivate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "reason": "Manual operator deactivation for distributed transaction demo"
}

### 32.4 Poll claim until status becomes CLOSED_NO_PENALTY
GET {{gatewayBaseUrl}}/api/claims/{{createClaim.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}

### 32.5 Inspect timeline
GET {{gatewayBaseUrl}}/api/claims/{{createClaim.response.body.$.id}}/timeline
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}
